# Phase 18 Remoting ErrorSource identity equality

- Recorded: 2026-10-24 10:07:26 UTC
- Workspace: `/Users/bruce.tsai/Projects/trio/rocketmq-classic`
- Branch: `phase/18-phase-18-compatibility-closure`
- Code revision: `1e928372` (`fix(remoting): match Java throwable identity equality`)
- Pinned Java source: RocketMQ 5.5.1,
  `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`

## Change

`ErrorSource` previously compared wrapped causes by rendered source-chain text.
Java `Throwable.equals` inherits identity equality from `Object`. Rust now
compares the identity of its shared `Arc` error object, so clones remain equal
and separate causes with the same message compare unequal. A regression covers
both `ErrorSource` and derived `TransportError` equality. The request-failure
classification test now checks the mapped variant, address, and cause message
instead of constructing a second error object and expecting identity equality.

The Remoting inventory and known-differences note now reflect this mapping. The
older release-checklist entry is retained as historical evidence and
superseded by the new follow-up entry.

